WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Rugby 
Team

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:02.980
A training camp at school?

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.630
It'll be for five days during Golden Week.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.860
We've already gotten 
our adviser's approval.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.990
All right! Yeah!

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.960
That sounds fun!

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.990
Should we bring our futons?

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:14.240
We'll be practicing from morning to night.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.950
Did our adviser say he was coming, too?

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.010
I see.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.250
When was the last time he even showed up?

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.460
In any case, it's less than two weeks
until the training camp.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.500
We'll keep practicing hard till then.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.970
Yes, sir!

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.710
We did plan to go away 
for our training camp...

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.520
But with <i>our </i>adviser...

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.520
If only we had someone to lead us properly...

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.890
G-Gion? What on earth are you doing?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.570
I was sleeping, sir.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.380
Why were you buried under that pile?

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.150
Raita did this, didn't he?

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.580
In any case, let's do what we can.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.460
Oh. Yeah.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.140
We're leaving, Gion.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.220
Laters.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.260
What were they talking about?

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.060
I'm so sleepy.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:08.010
<b>Episode 5
What's Lacking</b>

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.770
When did you guys wake up this morning?

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:06.530
Five.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.140
I got up at four.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.830
Quit wasting time!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:10.960
Y-Yes, sir!

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.170
Our five-day training camp begins today.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.530
I'm sure all of you are aware

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.590
of what our team is lacking 
after our match against Keijo.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.100
If you have any thoughts 
or suggestions, share them.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.350
First-years, don't be shy.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.350
Let's make this a fruitful training camp.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.850
Split up into forwards and backs.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.860
Backs, we'll start with running passes.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.310
Here we go.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.290
Here.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:39.940
Here.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.340
This is too easy.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.280
Are you messing with me, you turd?

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.500
No fighting!

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:53.830
If you're really a wing, you'd better 
not drop the ball, even if it kills you.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.580
I'll teach you how to catch. Come over here!

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:59.580
What? Do you even know how to teach?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:02.220
Shut up, you loser! 
Hurry up and come over here!

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.820
That's not how the upperclassmen 
were throwing it.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.060
You're holding the ball wrong.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:16.060
Let me see it.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.380
Yes, sir.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.520
You start by holding the ball like this.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.320
Yes, sir.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.290
Then, you throw the ball like this.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.820
The second-years are 
teaching the first-years.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:24.820
I see.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.820
Next!

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:30.580
Yes, sir.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.250
Your head's dropping!

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.210
It's only the first day, you know!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:41.890
Sir...

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.390
Sumiaki.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.390
I'm glad you're still playing rugby.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.400
I had my doubts about the game, 
but I couldn't give it up.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.400
It's too much fun.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.930
Your team has a lot of 
interesting characters in it.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.460
Good luck to both of us.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.180
Yeah.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.100
Next time, we definitely won't lose.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.170
One more time.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.020
You're all too inefficient.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.450
Sekizan...

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.800
Um, do you work here at the school?

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.790
Which one of you is Gion?

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:00.290
What?

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.540
He invited me here.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.370
He wants me to coach you.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.390
Oh, yeah! I <i>did</i> contact you.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:16.250
It's because the captain said something
about needing someone to lead us.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:20.520
This guy came up when I searched for 
"rugby coach," so I dropped him a line.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.270
Apparently, he played for the national team.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.150
I'm Komori Shingo.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.490
I retired this year and 
have nothing better to do.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:32.510
Who's the captain?

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.490
Me.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.000
What are you, stupid?

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.680
I've been watching you 
practice since this morning.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:49.340
You've been at it for four hours 
without taking any real breaks.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:54.100
You ever look at the clock? 
Or even your teammates?

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.650
Must be tough having this 
taskmaster for a captain.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.540
I'm supposed to start coaching you today,

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:16.660
but I've been watching you practice
since Gion e-mailed me two weeks ago.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.660
All you do is make them run like idiots
and crash into each other.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:24.830
Captain, you're the only one
with any energy left by the end of it.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:31.660
If you keep this up, you'll lose half
your members by summer vacation.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:38.560
Um, it sounds like one of our first-years 
contacted you without talking to us first...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.930
He didn't even get permission 
from our adviser.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.620
So I think you should leave for—

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.620
Mutsumi!

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.630
Captain, how many years
have you been playing rugby?

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.360
Three.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.060
I knew it.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:58.870
You've got a solid build,
but your movements are terrible.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.290
You've never had any 
proper coaching, have you?

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.070
The only thing I can commend you on
is that you don't make excuses.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.930
Looks like I'm not welcome here.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.100
I'm leaving.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.710
Wait!

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:23.330
What is it that we're lacking?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.040
Sekizan...

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.610
What were you planning on doing 
during this training camp?

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:36.250
Two weeks ago, we lost a game.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.370
The gap in physicality between
the teams was particularly large,

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.860
so I thought we could work on that...

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.620
Were your opponents all big guys?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:45.530
Yes.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:52.530
Captain, you and that big guy 
over there are on defense.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.970
These two little guys will be on offense.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.460
"Little"?

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.380
Try to make it past them.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:08.610
You big lugs won't be able to stop them.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.610
The rules are simple.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:15.190
You'll try to run past each other
within a ten by ten meter area.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:17.610
If the offensive pairing 
scores a try, they win.

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.870
They've got an amateur 
in Gion on their side.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.120
Between the captain and Iwashi,
there won't be any room to get past them.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:27.120
It's our first time going up 
against each other, Sekki.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.160
Don't underestimate us.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.880
Sometimes, the bullet hurts 
more than the cannonball.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.630
Give me your best shot.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:38.890
Begin.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:42.350
<i>A pass...</i>

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.810
<i>No, it's a fake out!</i>

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.590
Whoops! You figured me out?

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.340
One more time!

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:54.740
You're not getting through!

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.700
Gotcha! I was actually going for a pass!

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:11.530
You apparently can't catch, 
so when the pass comes...

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.220
...headbutt the ball.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.350
Try!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.200
We did it! All right!

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:31.960
Hey, wait! Wasn't that a knock-on?

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.150
That's against the rules!

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:38.650
Section 12 of the rule book
only mentions the hand or arm.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:42.120
A ball headed forward is still live.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:46.160
Quit complaining when
you don't even know the rules.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:50.120
Switch sides.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.180
Now, the big guys will be on offense.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:58.780
<i>If I get the ball,
I'll pass it to the captain.</i>

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.180
Hey, Tree Trunk.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.880
Man, you're as apprehensive as ever.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:07.270
You still can't go for a play
unless someone kicks you in the ass?

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:11.650
If that's how you approach rugby,
just quit already.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.690
Quit flapping your gums.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.400
Begin.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:17.830
Come at me!

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:25.250
<i>Thanks to you, I remembered 
how fun rugby can be.</i>

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:30.160
<i>But there are lots of things 
about rugby you still don't know.</i>

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:34.670
<i>You're always doing something reckless
or running your mouth.</i>

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.690
That's not good enough.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.670
<i>He's too high.</i>

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.170
<i>I can knock him down.</i>

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.550
<i>Today, I'll teach you—</i>

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:48.200
You have good form,
but you're starting too low.

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:52.050
Get as close as you can 
while you're upright.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:55.810
Utilize your speed by crouching just 
before you run into your opponent...

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.100
...and stab.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.820
Yeah!

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.280
Huh? He crossed the line.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.760
All right! I made a tackle!

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.220
But they scored a try.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:22.940
It's a good thing your body's so long.
But now, you see how it is.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.390
You're lucky you reached the line that time.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:29.900
You rely on the strength of your arms
to drag your opponents down.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.990
You squeak through situations 
by using your height.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:35.500
Because your plays rely on your strength,

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:39.150
it doesn't work against opponents 
stronger than yourselves.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.200
Use your head.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:46.910
Rugby isn't a contest of strength.

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:49.880
Don't blame your frailty
on your physical abilities.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.910
There are plenty of things 
you guys are lacking.

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.680
Resting is part of practice, too.

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.500
Meet on the field in three hours' time.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.930
Go eat and take a nap.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.950
<b>Stab</b>

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:15.940
<b>Midget-senpai,
that hurt!</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:19.940
<b>Home Economics Room</b>

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.550
I'm hungry!

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.440
Boys!

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:26.390
Did you wash your hands?

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:28.250
I'm making something 
right now, so be patient!

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.000
Hey, it's Kamo-san!

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.580
Damn it, Hyosu! Help me!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.460
She and Hachioji-san came to cook.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:34.690
Hey, wait!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.900
Oh, my. There's someone even 
smaller than Raita on the team.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.660
You don't want to stay that way forever.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:44.050
You should eat more.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.500
Iwashimizu-kun, you've grown so much.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:48.000
Hello.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.220
Mu's told me all about you.

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.460
Here.

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:54.180
Oh, that's too much.

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.060
Thanks for the food.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.560
Thanks for the food!

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.570
You asshole, that's mine!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.330
More!

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:12.410
Raita! You can get your 
own second helping, idiot!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.460
I never get any taller because 
you're always bashing me down!

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.500
That Komori guy...

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.690
I don't like him much.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.920
Yeah, neither do I.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.990
<b>Rugby Practice Techniques</b>

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.990
Taku, you're not sleeping?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.780
Taku? Taku?

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:34.360
Oh, no...

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.660
Are you going to make him our coach?

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:48.540
I've never been coached like that
by our adviser or the upperclassmen.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.780
Passing and Catching

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.780
The most 
fundamental 
of all 
fundamentals! 
Important!!

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:56.780
It made me happy.

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:07.550
We can become stronger.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:12.920
That was a good nap.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.850
What's he going to make us do this afternoon?

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.890
He's scary.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.420
Quit complaining.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.230
I'm sure we'll learn a lot.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.750
If you say so...

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:27.900
All right!

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:31.860
Whether we're doing tackles or 
a hundred running passes, bring it on!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.170
What <i>is</i> this?

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.410
Oh, you're here.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.990
Start warming up.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.990
Wh-What the heck is this?!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.920
Let's start afternoon practice.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.950
Move your bodies, not your mouths.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.990
We'll start at 150 centimeters.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:54.430
Throw running passes low enough 
that they don't hit the line.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:57.930
O-Okay, then.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:00.770
Come on!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:01.240
Too close!

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.190
Where are you aiming—

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.150
Next.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.040
This is too easy!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.420
Hey, short stuff.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.630
You guys will start by
getting used to crouching low.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:36.640
At the same time, you'll dodge posts 
placed at five meter intervals.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.890
A low profile and peripheral vision...

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:44.100
If you want to win with a smaller team, 
you'll have to master these skills first.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.970
Keep it up.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:54.610
Take a three-minute break.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:58.250
I'm twice as tired from 
using my brain so much.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.130
This is fun.

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:02.910
Next, we'll split into forwards and backs.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.620
I'll coach the forwards first.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.530
Everyone start with the turtle.

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:08.630
What?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:13.510
Form is everything for forwards.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.630
Master it.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:16.810
Stomachs down.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.260
Don't let your heads drop.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.640
Butt cheeks pointing toward the sky.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:21.890
Can you hear me?

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:24.210
Don't slack off.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.480
Bastard!

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:29.180
Your neck muscles are important, too.

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:36.390
Remember the form you used 
during the string exercise.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.700
You can go lower.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.870
That's it. Good. Next.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:44.090
Hey, front row.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.930
Get in scrum formation.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.710
Hey, you. Come here.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:53.820
What's going on?

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.980
Who is it?!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.640
We're collapsing! We're collapsing!

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.220
That's not enough to crush you.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:05.730
You're the front row.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:08.710
Aren't you the strongest guys on the team?

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.730
Dammit!

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.490
You're the team's front line.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:17.800
You've got to be strong enough to 
carry the entire team on your backs.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:26.530
Then, bring any one of 'em 
here and we'll carry 'em!

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:28.180
Good. Captain, come here.

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:28.750
What?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.680
We can't carry him!

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.750
No way! No <i>way!</i>

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:37.760
Next, we'll bring in the backs 
and practice some offensive scrums.

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:40.500
Hirota, are you okay?

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.640
Y-Yeah...

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.560
Begin.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:52.580
Oh, sorry.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:54.870
Hey...

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.650
You'd better not be messing around.

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:07.630
Sorry. Could we try that again?

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:10.080
What? You little...

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:21.780
I've been wanting to say this 
to the backs for a while...

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.600
Quit dropping the ball all the time!

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:26.530
Especially right after a scrum!

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.390
It pisses me off so much,
I want to kill you guys!

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:29.980
Now, now.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:37.060
I'm sure scrums are hard, 
but the backs have to run really far.

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:39.360
That makes us even.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.380
It's not the same!

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:43.870
You guys try forming a scrum!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.310
Just how hard do you think it is?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.130
Come on, let me see you do it!

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:49.580
Hey.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.590
Hirota.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:54.500
No fighting.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:20:01.050
I wouldn't be able to step 
around a player or outrun someone.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:06.270
I thought about what I could bring 
to the team. So I worked out,

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:11.020
learned to handle the ball,
 and became a hooker.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:16.060
We're all filling in the gaps 
in each other's game.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:20.070
And aren't we supposed to carry everyone?

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.820
Even the guys who drop the ball
from time to time?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.980
You can't do that if you're fighting.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:37.320
Someone once said they wished 
backs understood that...

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:40.460
when the forwards 
retreat ten centimeters,

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.680
the backs have to retreat a whole meter.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:49.680
And because that's how we play, 
let's all give everything we've got.

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:55.940
But Oharano, you should understand 
scrums better, so let's give it a shot.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:58.440
What?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.440
You can do it!

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.810
Hey, wait! Wait!

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.810
You can borrow my headgear.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:04.100
No, please! I can't!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:07.450
Looks like some of you already understand.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:17.960
It's hot, it's cramped, and it stinks!

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:28.190
We were kids.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.850
We've been practicing without 
an adviser since our first year.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:42.360
Maybe we thought we could 
do everything ourselves.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:52.870
K-Komori-san!

00:21:57.310 --> 00:22:01.000
Tomorrow... what time should 
we meet on the field?

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:07.770
Five.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.220
Yes, sir!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next Time: "Giving Everything You've Got"</b>

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:48.780
Next time: "Giving Everything You've Got."
